dard practice in mature engineering organizations. The key question from my perspective: does this actually accelerate or decelerate our prototyping cycles?\n\nI'll lean toward approve with moderate-to-good promise score. The technical approach is sound (it's basically a structured logging middleware), it addresses real regulatory requirements, and preventing redundant work across teams is good engineering practice. My concern is the \"unified\" aspect potentially over-abstracting before we need to, but the modular design mitigates that.\n\nI'll give it around 62-70. It's technically viable, addresses a real problem, but has execution risk in terms of fitting our prototyping cadence and the abstraction may not match all future use cases well enough.\n",
