r may not be sufficient for all Article 12 sub-requirements, but as a foundational layer it's the right architectural decision and the most resource-efficient path to compliance.\n\nI'd rate this highly from my vantage point. It's the kind of infrastructure investment that amortizes well across multiple projects and preserves scientific capacity. I'd give it around 82-85. It's not a 90+ because there are real concerns about whether a pure middleware layer covers all the specific Article 12(3) requirements without project-specific add-ons, and the centralized immutable store has ongoing cost implications that need to be budgeted. But as an architectural foundation for resource-efficient compliance, it's excellent.\n\nLet me settle on: approve, promise 84.\n",
