hinking about standardization.\n\nI think this is technically viable (the core pattern works), but from a prototyping speed perspective, I have reservations about the \"unified across ALL pipelines\" scope creating a bottleneck. That said, without this kind of infrastructure, each project would handle logging ad-hoc, which creates compliance risk and technical debt.\n\nI'll approve it because the technical approach is sound and necessary, but I'll give a moderate-to-high promise score reflecting that while viable, the execution scope and prototyping impact are concerns. The \"intercept model calls\" pattern is proven, the CI/CD integration makes sense for deployment configuration, and having a consistent logging interface reduces per-project burden long-term. My main reservation is the upfront investment before it's useful and the potential to slow down experimental work if not designed with opt-in/dev modes.\n\nI'd say around 72-78 promise. Technically very viable (high confidence it can be built), but the prototyping speed impact is a real concern that tempers enthusiasm. The \"across all pipelines\" scope is ambitious and could mean long lead times before researchers see benefit.\n",
