throughout lifetime?\n\nMy decision: This is a reasonable and useful initiative that supports the broader compliance framework (Recital 71, Art. 11 technical documentation), though it's not a direct implementation of Article 12's logging requirements per se. It reduces administrative burden while improving compliance posture. From my vantage point, I'd lean toward approving it because:\n1. It addresses a genuine regulatory obligation (technical documentation must be comprehensive and up-to-date)\n2. Automation reduces error risk in compliance-critical records\n3. Pulling from MLflow ensures data provenance\n4. It supports audit readiness\n\nHowever, my concerns:\n- Vagueness about which specific regulatory requirements it maps to\n- Doesn't address the actual logging (runtime event capture) that Art. 12 mandates\n- \"EU AI Act standards\" is not a precise reference — I'd want a compliance mapping document\n\nI think I'll approve this with moderate confidence, maybe around 65-70 on the promise scale. It's useful and addresses real needs, but it's somewhat incomplete from a strict Article 12 perspective and lacks specificity in its regulatory mapping.\n\nLet me settle on: Approve, promise score ~68.\n",
