ema\n4. CI/CD integration is nice-to-have but not the core value\n\nOverall: This is a solid direction that I'd want to pursue, with modifications. The technical approach is viable, it does address Article 12(1)-(3), and it has real benefits for prototyping speed by eliminating boilerplate. But the \"immutable ledger\" and \"forces\" language suggests a one-size-fits-all rigidity that could work against rapid iteration. I'd approve it as a direction but with the understanding that implementation would need flexibility for different system architectures and a dev/prod mode distinction.\n\nI'll rate this around 68-72. It's technically sound, addresses the regulatory requirement directly, and has genuine prototyping speed benefits. But the rigidity concerns and the \"immutable ledger\" over-engineering concern me somewhat from a pure prototyping velocity standpoint. I'd say 70.\n",
