rivacy on the audit trail itself.\n- Secure multi-party computation for audit logging is technically fascinating but operationally impractical and would likely NOT satisfy a regulator's need to inspect logs during a compliance check or incident investigation.\n\nMy assessment: This proposal, as framed, risks building a non-compliant system. The \"privacy-preserving\" approach to regulatory audit logs contradicts the core purpose of Article 12 (traceability, verifiability). While data protection is important, it should be addressed through proper governance rather than by degrading the fidelity of mandatory records. Approving this would commit scarce resources to a research direction that, if implemented as described, could create compliance liability rather than resolve it.\n\nDecision: Reject.\n",
