latory requirement, it doesn't leverage existing infrastructure, and the resource commitment would be disproportionate to the compliance benefit. The legitimate needs within Article 12 could be met more efficiently through targeted adaptation of existing tools rather than a ground-up \"comprehensive system.\"\n\nPromise score: From my vantage point, there's some kernel of valid need (better provenance tracking helps compliance), but the specific proposal as framed is a resource sink. I'd say around 25-30 - there's value in the direction but this specific implementation approach and scope would be a poor use of our limited resources.\n",
