cise dataset versioning per query is a strong differentiator in regulated markets.\n\n**Risk assessment:**\n- If we don't implement this, we have a clear gap in Article 12(3)(b) compliance for Annex III 1(a) systems (biometrics-related).\n- The technical approach (dataset hashes + timestamps) is well-established and low-risk to implement correctly.\n- This is a \"table stakes\" requirement — not innovative but absolutely necessary.\n\n**My assessment:** This is a clear, targeted, legally-motivated proposal that addresses a specific compliance obligation with a technically sound approach. From my compliance perspective, this is essential infrastructure. I should approve it. The promise score should be high because it directly closes a regulatory gap with low implementation risk and clear legal mapping.\n\nI'll give it around 90-92. It's very strong but not perfect — I'd want to see how it integrates with the broader logging architecture (covering all of Article 12(3)), and I'd want to confirm the \"dataset hash\" approach is sufficient for what regulators mean by \"reference database\" (could they want a human-readable name too?). But those are implementation details, not reasons to reject.\n",
