p to date throughout the lifetime\" requirement suggest this pipeline should also capture deployment/runtime metadata, which extends the scope but is still technically feasible.\n\n**Overall assessment from my vantage point:**\nThis is a strong, technically viable proposal that directly addresses a real engineering pain point (audit prep) while improving prototyping speed (no separate compliance documentation sprints). The core technology is well-understood and composable from existing tools. The main risk is scope creep into trying to auto-generate narrative content that inherently requires human input, but the pipeline architecture itself is sound and buildable. I'd estimate a functional prototype in 6-10 weeks with a small team.\n\nThis clears my bar for technical viability and prototyping speed/quality improvement. I'll approve it.\n\nPromise score: This is very aligned with my domain concerns. The technical approach is sound, the tools exist or are easily buildable, and it directly reduces friction in our development workflow. I'd say 82 — high confidence in feasibility and value, slight deduction for the scope ambiguity around \"comprehensive\" documentation and the Annex III(1)(a) runtime logging requirements that extend beyond pure CI/CD integration.\n",
